1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,848
CHAPTER 1 — THE ARTICLE HE NEVER FINISHED

2
00:00:04,148 --> 00:00:13,582
Frank Herbert was a journalist and short-story writer. In Oregon, he saw something that wouldn't let him go: the sand moved like a very slow sea.

3
00:00:13,762 --> 00:00:20,857
He began reading about deserts, ecology, religion, and power. He spent six years writing.

4
00:00:21,037 --> 00:00:26,395
Out of that came a desert planet, where water is worth more than any treasure.

5
00:00:26,575 --> 00:00:35,179
The story came out first as a serial in a science fiction magazine, between 1963 and 1965.

6
00:00:35,829 --> 00:00:39,678
The hardest part was still ahead: turning it into a book.
